[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Welcome to the Anti-gravity A1 guide, a step-by-step tutorial for drone-based 360° capture. Focus on three key factors for a high-quality 3D reconstruction in Splatika. Achieve a smooth flight without sudden movements. Ensure full'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'altitude coverage with low, mid, and high passes. Maintain a stable light and scene with fixed exposure and minimal movement. In step one, shooting time and location. Fly during the day in good'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'weather, avoiding rain and strong wind. For the scene, eliminate moving objects like cars or people. For safety, start from an open area with reliable GNSS and obey all no fly rules. Fix all settings'

[00:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'before take off. Step two, equipment setup. Check your drone\'s lenses, propellers, landing gear, and ensure the battery is fully charged. The micro SD card must have free space and all'

[00:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'firmware must be up to date. Charge the goggles and grip controller. Most importantly, set the flight mode to cinematic or C for a slow and smooth flight. Step three, basic camera settings. Switch to pro mode for manual'

[01:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'control. Use a fixed shutter speed, typically 1/2000 s or 1/1000 s for lower light. Set the EV to -0.7 and the white balance to a fixed taste,'

[01:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'not auto. The ISO can be set to auto. Do not use auto shutter as flicker will ruin the clip. Step four, shooting specification settings. For daytime bright light, use 8K at 30 FPS for'

[01:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'maximum detail. For evening or lower light, select 5.2K at 60 FPS. The higher frame rate reduces motion blur when light is limited. Step five, advanced shooting settings. Set the video'

[01:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'encoding format to H.265 for best compression. Set the bit rate to high for maximum image quality. H.265 and high bit rate are mandatory for optimal frame quality in Splatika.'

[01:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Step six, movement rules. Before recording, select a clear starting point, confirm scene stability, and switch to cinematic mode. Move slowly and evenly, avoiding sudden yaw, jerks, or altitude jumps. Do not use the 360'

[02:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'dial button. Maintain a safe distance from obstacles, and return close to the starting point before stopping the recording. Step seven, how close to fly. Fly as close as you safely can to capture more detail.'

[02:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'For facades, use a close and safe zigzag path followed by a wider path. For wide scenes, combine a close path with a wider path for detail and context. Never sacrifice safety if obstacles are'

[02:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'present. This illustrates a snake orbit pattern, combining vertical and lateral movement for full surface coverage with overlapping viewpoints. This close fly-through demonstrates'

[02:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'maintaining a steady path near the subject to capture fine surface detail. Step eight, full coverage, four passes. Do not stop recording between passes. Pass one establishes mid-altitude orbit.'

[03:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Pass two is a fill-in using a snake or zigzag pattern. Pass three is a wide high pass for context. Pass four is a reverse return, flying back from a different angle to close the loop. Keep'

[03:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'one continuous clip. For building facades, use a vertical snake trajectory, treating the surface like a flat wall. Start low, fly up, slide sideways, fly down, slide sideways, and repeat to cover the entire area in a'

[03:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'lawnmower pattern. For cylindrical objects like sculptures or trees, use a spiral or cylindrical snake. Start low and close, then spiral upward slowly, completing multiple loops to cover the subject from bottom to top, every angle.'

[03:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'For houses, follow four stages. Start with a low perimeter orbit at 1 to 1.5 m for ground level detail. Next, a mid perimeter orbit at 2 to 3 m captures the main facade. Third, an overhead snake'

[03:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'covers the roof. Finally, a wide spiral descent with a radius twice the house extent captures the surrounding context. To capture trajectories using Sky Genie, first plan your shape, whether it\'s a'

[04:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'vertical snake or a spiral. Next, drop 8 to 20 waypoints at corners and inflection points, aiming the gimbal before locking each one. Finally, launch the automatic flight for smooth'

[04:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'arc-filled movements without manual corrections. For clip length, optimal is 3 to 5 minutes, and acceptable is up to 6 minutes. Before uploading, check that the main subject is captured from low, mid, and high viewpoints. Ensure there\'s'

[04:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a loop-closing path, no motion blur, and no sudden exposure or white balance jumps. To upload to Splatica, copy the source file from the drone or micro SD card, then upload the raw INSP file directly'

[04:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to app.splatica.com. Remember, do not export to MP4, auto edit, reframe, stabilize, transcode, or rename the raw source file before'

[04:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'uploading. Avoid common errors like flying in sport mode. Always use cinematic mode. Ensure you have more than one automated move for full coverage. For low light, slow down or use 5.2K/60 fps'

[05:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'with a fixed shutter to prevent motion blur. Always capture low, mid, and high altitudes, and return close to the starting point. Use this final control sheet before flying. Check your drone.'

[05:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Clean lenses, checked propellers, charged battery, free micro SD, and cinematic flight mode. Check the scene. Acceptable weather, stable light, no strong wind, and no dangerous obstacles'

[05:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'or moving subjects. For shooting, confirm fixed white balance, a shutter speed of 1/1000 s or 1/2000 s, fixed EV with auto ISO, low/mid/high'

[05:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'coverage, and a loop closing return path.'
